      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to think of a way, but there\u0027s no easy way to figure this out.\n\nI do have a couple of alternatives that may be worth considering.\nThere are a couple of other pesky defines in gpio_map.h that use a redefinition to GPIO_UNIMPLEMENTED to essentially null out  a GPIO reference in common code (and GPIO_ENTERING_RW is another example of that). My first inclination was to use Kconfig to properly option the code, but it gets messy (the ones in question is the skyrim/guybrush redefinition of GPIO_PCH_SYS_PWROK and the intelrvp redefinition of GPIO_EN_PP5000).\nI could create a named-gpios-unimplemented compatible and have these GPIOs added to that. I could also used that for GPIO_ENTERING_RW as well.\nAlternatively I could make the gpio phandle in named-gpios optional, and if it is missing, use GPIO_UNIMPLEMENTED (-1) for it - I prefer the former approach, since that seems more obvious and cleaner.\n\nIt seemms a bit of a crude approach to redefine these GPIOs to GPIO_UNIMPLEMENTED, but this is mostly to solve legacy issues, so I think I have come around to seeing that this may be the best compromise. Thoughts welcome.",
      "parentUuid": "b684898d_bd2f000e",
      "revId": "4f421c06be4007334cb040fa4db41a84a9d8807d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
